one of the entertaining things about Moorcock's fiction is that often,
characters from different books will make guest appearances. in the Elric
books, Arioch is Elric's patron and often helps him out; in the first of the
Corum books, Arioch is the Knight of the Swords, his sworn enemy. this gets
a little confusing when you appreciate that Elric and Corum are incarnations
of the Eternal Champion and theoretically posess the same soul.

Moorcock did a series of excellent stories set at the End of Time, where the
residents have the power to create anything they can imagine, which they use
to entertain each other. in "Elric at the End of Time", Elric is transported
to this period, and the contrast between the gentle denizens of the End of
Time and Elric's moepygoth doom-and-gloom is one of the funniest things i've
read. Arioch appeared in this book, too.

